diff --git a/src/lotus_v2/avalanche_peer_test/README.md b/src/lotus_v2/avalanche_peer_test/README.md
index 1245d7f5eefad0ba63ad814b3a2e3cf205612e3b..59d80d28fe3562e531545045fcce310208841234 100644
--- a/src/lotus_v2/avalanche_peer_test/README.md
+++ b/src/lotus_v2/avalanche_peer_test/README.md
@@ -80,3 +80,22 @@ remaining members. Removed advertised proofs produce notfound. Peers that never
 request another page cannot receive further discovery information. Tests cover
 65-proof stable catalogs, mutation between pages, subsequent cycle refresh,
 removed-proof notfound, and local hello/session key mismatch before queuing.
+
+Connection outcomes are explicit. Every application checks the live negotiated
+feature, nonzero payload limit and transcript before callbacks or mutation.
+A removed or closed connection returns UnknownPeer; a live connection whose
+negotiated limit cannot fit an outgoing message returns Rejected. Both outcomes
+terminate only that peer. Transient action pressure returns Backpressure before
+application callbacks and retains the exact notice for retry. Local encoding,
+signing, response invariants and local bounds remain LocalFailure. Multiple
+responses are checked together before any enqueue, so permanent oversize cannot
+leave a fitting prefix queued. Pump retains its front action on dispatcher Busy;
+its owner disconnects terminal targets and releases their actions before the
+next healthy target advances.
+
+The native tests cover an actual retained dispatcher Application after Remove,
+a directly closed Transport exposing an optional zero limit, a live 128-byte
+negotiation, mixed fitting/oversized response batches, transient pressure with
+exactly one callback after retry, genuine local callback failure, and two live
+connections sharing an action queue through terminal-target cleanup. These are
+connection lifecycle checks; nine-node native quorum acceptance is separate.
